  <data key="d6">FASHION-MNIST CLASSIFICATION USING CNN</data>
  <data key="d5">2023</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.56726/irjmets42990</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
  <data key="d9">The realm of fashion has consistently held a significant position of importance within our daily lives.Furthermore, it serves a pivotal function in the existence of all individuals.In the present study, Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) are utilized for the purpose of training on diverse fashion style images and subsequently predicting them with a high degree of accuracy.The application of deep learning has been extensively implemented in various domains in recent times.A Convolutional Neural Network (CNN) is a type of deep neural network that is widely acclaimed for its ability to provide highly precise predictions and classifications when confronted with complex real-world scenarios.Clothing manufacturers have resorted to utilizing the services of CNN to address a myriad of challenges</data>
</node>
<node id="paper:W3130921877">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Classifying Garments from Fashion-MNIST Dataset Through CNNs</data>
  <data key="d6">Classifying Garments from Fashion-MNIST Dataset Through CNNs</data>
  <data key="d5">2021</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.25046/aj0601109</data>
  <data key="d8">47</data>
  <data key="d9">Online fashion market is constantly growing, and an algorithm capable of identifying garments can help companies in the clothing sales sector to understand the profile of potential buyers and focus on sales targeting specific niches, as well as developing campaigns based on the taste of customers and improve user experience.Artificial Intelligence approaches able to understand and label humans' clothes are necessary, and can be used to improve sales, or better understanding users.Convolutional Neural Network models have been shown efficiency in image c1assification.This paper presents four different Convolutional Neural Networks models that used Fashion-MNIST dataset.Fashion-MNIST is a dataset made to help researchers finding models to classify this kind of product such as clothes, and the</data>
