  <data key="d9">Prompt Engineering and Corruption Robustness Evaluation for CLIP Zero-Shot Image Classification on CIFAR-100 A systematic study of prompt engineering and image corruption robustness for CLIP ViT-B/32 zero-shot classification on CIFAR-100. What this release includes: Evaluation of 13 natural language prompt templates for zero-shot classification, measuring Top-1 and Top-5 accuracy Robustness testing across 9 corruption types (Gaussian/motion blur, Gaussian/salt-pepper noise, random occlusion, cutout, brightness, contrast, JPEG compression) at 3 severity levels Linear probe baseline (logistic regression on CLIP features) for fine-tuned model comparison 15+ publication-quality visualizations including heatmaps, resilience rankings, severity curves, and a 4-panel CLIP vs. linear probe comparis</data>
