  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.2174/0123520965348453250226080233</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">Introduction: Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) and deep learning algorithms have significantly advanced image processing and classification. This study compares three CNN architectures VGG-16, ResNet-50, and ResNet-18, and evaluates their performance on the CIFAR- 100 and MNIST datasets. Training time is prioritized as a critical metric, along with test accuracy and training loss, under varying hardware configurations (NVIDIA-GPU and Intel-CPU). Methods: Experiments were conducted on an Ubuntu 22.04 system using the PyTorch framework. The hardware configurations included an NVIDIA GeForce GTX 1660 Super GPU and an Intel Core i5-10400 CPU. The CIFAR-100 dataset, containing 60,000 color images across 100 classes, and the MNIST dataset, comprising 70,000 grayscale images, were used for be</data>
