  <data key="d1">Selective ECC protection of quantized neural networks (INT-8 ResNet-18 / CIFAR-10 and MobileNetV2 / CIFAR-100): models, trained agents, learned and rule-based protection policies, held-out fault-injection results and layer-interaction data</data>
  <data key="d6">Selective ECC protection of quantized neural networks (INT-8 ResNet-18 / CIFAR-10 and MobileNetV2 / CIFAR-100): models, trained agents, learned and rule-based protection policies, held-out fault-injection results and layer-interaction data</data>
  <data key="d5">2026</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23054819</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">Companion data for the manuscript Learned or Ranked? A Cost-Matched, Held-Out Benchmark of Selective ECC Protection for Quantized Neural Networks Under Realistic Memory Faults. Contents: (1) the BN-folded, per-tensor symmetric INT-8 ResNet-18 (CIFAR-10) whose stored weights are faulted in every experiment; (2) all 156 protection policies selected by 13 allocation methods (QMIX, VDN, IQL, a non-monotonic mixer, three sequential DQN variants, greedy forward/backward, genetic algorithm, simulated annealing, cross-entropy method, random search), 4 trade-off weights x 3 seeds each, with their held-out accuracy and protection cost; (3) the held-out evaluation report (10 fault-seed blocks x 10 draws on the 10,000-image CIFAR-10 test set), matched-cost comparisons with eight ranking rules, paired </data>
</node>
