<node id="paper:W4394643157">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Dual Path Networks</data>
  <data key="d6">Dual Path Networks</data>
  <data key="d5">2017</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.1707.01629</data>
  <data key="d8">677</data>
  <data key="d9">In this work, we present a simple, highly efficient and modularized Dual Path Network (DPN) for image classification which presents a new topology of connection paths internally. By revealing the equivalence of the state-of-the-art Residual Network (ResNet) and Densely Convolutional Network (DenseNet) within the HORNN framework, we find that ResNet enables feature re-usage while DenseNet enables new features exploration which are both important for learning good representations. To enjoy the benefits from both path topologies, our proposed Dual Path Network shares common features while maintaining the flexibility to explore new features through dual path architectures. Extensive experiments on three benchmark datasets, ImagNet-1k, Places365 and PASCAL VOC, clearly demonstrate superior perf</data>
</node>
