<node id="paper:W4416184404">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">CSF-Net: Context-Semantic Fusion Network for Large Mask Inpainting</data>
  <data key="d6">CSF-Net: Context-Semantic Fusion Network for Large Mask Inpainting</data>
  <data key="d5">2026</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.1109/wacv61042.2026.00800</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">In this paper, we propose a semantic-guided framework to address the challenging problem of large-mask image inpainting, where essential visual content is missing and contextual cues are limited. To compensate for the limited context, we leverage a pretrained Amodal Completion (AC) model to generate structure-aware candidates that serve as semantic priors for the missing regions. We introduce Context-Semantic Fusion Network (CSF-Net), a transformer-based fusion framework that fuses these candidates with contextual features to produce a semantic guidance image for image inpainting. This guidance improves inpainting quality by promoting structural accuracy and semantic consistency. CSF-Net can be seamlessly integrated into existing inpainting models without architectural changes and consiste</data>
</node>
