<node id="paper:W7165060532">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">FLOWER RECOGNITION SYSTEM</data>
  <data key="d6">FLOWER RECOGNITION SYSTEM</data>
  <data key="d5">2026</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.55248/gengpi.07.0626.15a07</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">Flower recognition is an important task in agriculture, ecological monitoring, and botanical research.The emergence of Convolutional Neural Networks (CNNs) has significantly enhanced the accuracy of image-based flower classification systems.This study presents a comparative analysis of three prominent CNN architectures: VGG-16, ResNet50, and GoogLeNet, for flower recognition.The models are evaluated using the Oxford 102 Flower Dataset and the ALXmamaev (2023) Flower Dataset, which offer diverse and challenging flower image collections.The methodology includes dataset preprocessing, model training, and performance evaluation.VGG-16 is examined for its effective feature extraction, ResNet50 for its residual learning mechanism, and GoogLeNet for its multi-scale feature representation through </data>
</node>
