<node id="paper:W7211906521">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Cross-AI Image-to-Image Roundtrip Corpus (companion data to arXiv:2606.14787), restricted bundle: CelebA-HQ-derived API outputs</data>
  <data key="d6">Cross-AI Image-to-Image Roundtrip Corpus (companion data to arXiv:2606.14787), restricted bundle: CelebA-HQ-derived API outputs</data>
  <data key="d5">2026</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22259971</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">Face-domain material from the corpus accompanying Vision-Encoder Behavioral Fingerprints of Image-to-Image Generative Models: A Training-Paradigm-Driven Taxonomy of Six Commercial APIs (Hill, 2026, arXiv:2606.14787): 888 image-to-image API outputs (6 APIs × up to 3 repeats; 12 calls were rejected by provider safety filters) derived from 50 CelebA-HQ-256 inputs. The 50 clean CelebA-HQ inputs are not included anywhere; fetch them by the source_id recorded in the open record's manifest.jsonl and verify with its verify_sha256.py --manifest. Perturbed inputs are not distributed. All metrics for these images are already public in the open record (DOI 10.5281/zenodo.22258270). Files. restricted_outputs.tar is deposited as 19 parts of 60 MB (restricted_outputs.tar.part-000 … .part-018). Download a</data>
</node>
