<node id="paper:W4294953517">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">ConvNeXt-Based Fine-Grained Image Classification and Bilinear Attention Mechanism Model</data>
  <data key="d6">ConvNeXt-Based Fine-Grained Image Classification and Bilinear Attention Mechanism Model</data>
  <data key="d5">2022</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.3390/app12189016</data>
  <data key="d8">45</data>
  <data key="d9">Thus far, few studies have been conducted on fine-grained classification tasks for the latest convolutional neural network ConvNeXt, and no effective optimization method has been made available. To achieve more accurate fine-grained classification, this paper proposes two attention embedding methods based on ConvNeXt network and designs a new bilinear CBAM; simultaneously, a multiscale, multi-perspective and all-around attention framework is proposed, which is then applied in ConvNeXt. Experimental verification shows that the accuracy rate of the improved ConvNeXt for fine-grained image classification reaches 87.8%, 91.2%, and 93.2% on fine-grained classification datasets CUB-200-2011, Stanford Cars, and FGVC Aircraft, respectively, showing increases of 2.7%, 0.3% and 0.4%, respectively, c</data>
</node>
