<node id="paper:W2896572288">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">PFNet: A Novel Part Fusion Network for Fine-Grained Image Categorization</data>
  <data key="d6">PFNet: A Novel Part Fusion Network for Fine-Grained Image Categorization</data>
  <data key="d5">2018</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.1109/bigmm.2018.8499094</data>
  <data key="d8">2</data>
  <data key="d9">Previous work in fine-grained image categorization focuses on integrating multiple deep CNN models or complicated attention mechanism, resulting in increasing cumbersome networks, and requiring expensive expert guidance. In this work, a part fusion network (PFNet) is proposed to fuse image parts for classification, which consists of a Fast R-CNN head to extract part features and a two-level classification network to encode part-level and image-level features simultaneously. Features from These two levels are trained with focal loss and cross-entropy loss respectively. By utilizing the focal loss, PFNet can learn more from hard examples of parts and thus generate more discriminative image features. Furthermore, it does not require extra part annotations and can be trained end to end. Experi</data>
</node>
<node id="author:jinlin guo">
  <data key="d0">Author</data>
  <data key="d1">Jinlin Guo</data>
</node>
