<node id="paper:W4417404964">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Performance Evaluation of Face Detection Algorithms on the WIDER FACE Dataset: A Comprehensive Comparison</data>
  <data key="d6">Performance Evaluation of Face Detection Algorithms on the WIDER FACE Dataset: A Comprehensive Comparison</data>
  <data key="d5">2025</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.1109/acroset66531.2025.11281211</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">Face detection is an important area of computer vision, and it finds application in many domains including security, human-computer interaction, and emotion recognition. Over the last decade, a variety of face detection algorithms have been proposed, and each has its own capabilities and shortcomings. It is important to learn about the differences between these algorithms so that the most appropriate method can be chosen for applications This paper provides a comparative analysis of different face detection algorithms, providing a thorough evaluation of their performance, computational complexity, robustness, and usability in real-world scenarios. Through the systematic comparison and evaluation of these algorithms, the paper determines the strengths and weaknesses of each algorithm and as</data>
</node>
