<node id="paper:W2155453525">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Open images of compactifications of the ray</data>
  <data key="d6">Open images of compactifications of the ray</data>
  <data key="d5">1991</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.1017/s0004972700029099</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
  <data key="d9">Let X be a compactification of the ray with the arc as remainder. The following characterisation of the open images of X is obtained: Let h: X → Y be an open onto map. If Y is not homeomorphic to [0, 1] or the one-point space, then h is a homeomorphism. In 1977 open images of the usual sin (1/x) continuum were characterised by Professor Sam B. Nadler.</data>
</node>
