  <data key="d8">832</data>
  <data key="d9">Most recent semantic segmentation methods adopt a fully-convolutional network (FCN) with an encoderdecoder architecture.The encoder progressively reduces the spatial resolution and learns more abstract/semantic visual concepts with larger receptive fields.Since context modeling is critical for segmentation, the latest efforts have been focused on increasing the receptive field, through either dilated/atrous convolutions or inserting attention modules.However, the encoder-decoder based FCN architecture remains unchanged.In this paper, we aim to provide an alternative perspective by treating semantic segmentation as a sequence-to-sequence prediction task.Specifically, we deploy a pure transformer (i.e., without convolution and resolution reduction) to encode an image as a sequence of patches</data>
