<node id="paper:W4385275388">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Vehicle Self-positioning system based on KITTI Database</data>
  <data key="d6">Vehicle Self-positioning system based on KITTI Database</data>
  <data key="d5">2023</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.1145/3594409.3594440</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">The main research of this paper is to design a multi-sensor fusion-based vehicle localisation algorithm. In order to achieve long-term robust and drift-free attitude estimation in autonomous driving, this paper proposes a method to fuse global position information with visual and inertial guidance measurement information based on a tightly coupled non-linear optimisation estimator. The vehicle position and the coordinate system of commonly used sensors are first analysed, then the GPS, IMU and visual odometry sensor models and data acquisition principles are divided and a multi-sensor fusion algorithm is designed. The multi-sensor fusion principle is firstly explored, and the multi-sensor fusion algorithm is proposed according to the multi-sensor fusion principle. After elaborating some cl</data>
</node>
<node id="author:weihan liu">
  <data key="d0">Author</data>
  <data key="d1">Weihan Liu</data>
</node>
<node id="paper:W4315488865">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Visual-Inertial Fusion on KITTI using MSF-EKF</data>
  <data key="d6">Visual-Inertial Fusion on KITTI using MSF-EKF</data>
  <data key="d5">2022</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.1109/icarcv57592.2022.10004344</data>
  <data key="d8">2</data>
  <data key="d9">In this article, we propose a loose-coupling approach between the accurate Parallax Beam (PB) algorithm and an Inertial Measurement Unit (IMU) for a robust, off-road and system agnostic navigation application. With the aim of achieving better robustness against image-shortage and motion-estimation errors while keeping PB accuracy, we propose the use of the Multi-Sensor Fusion Extended Kalman Filter (MSF-EKF). The latter uses asynchronous data provided by both the IMU and PB with different sampling rates to perform a high rate estimation able to ensure correct navigation during image shortage. The evaluation performed on the KITTI vision benchmark suite shows promising results with a good accuracy and is able to run with a sampling rate ten times faster than the sampling rate of Parallax Be</data>
</node>
