<node id="paper:W7131069840">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Descriptor: Occluded nuScenes Dataset (OccNuScenes)</data>
  <data key="d6">Descriptor: Occluded nuScenes Dataset (OccNuScenes)</data>
  <data key="d5">2026</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.1109/ieeedata.2026.3667122</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">Robust perception in automated driving requires reliable performance under adverse conditions, where sensors may be affected by partial failures or environmental occlusions. Although existing automated driving datasets inherently contain sensor noise and environmental variability, very few enable controlled, parameterised, and reproducible degradations across multiple sensing modalities. This gap limits the ability to systematically evaluate how perception and fusion architectures perform under well-defined adverse conditions. To address this limitation, we introduce the OccNuScenes Dataset, a novel extension of the widely used nuScenes benchmark. For the camera modality, we release both the full and mini versions, each with four occlusion types: two adapted from public implementations and</data>
</node>
