<node id="paper:W7214704911">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Natural Language Annotations for GSOT3D and NuScenes for LiDAR-Language Object Tracking</data>
  <data key="d6">Natural Language Annotations for GSOT3D and NuScenes for LiDAR-Language Object Tracking</data>
  <data key="d5">2026</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23033320</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">This dataset provides the natural language annotations generated in our work on LiDAR-language object tracking. The annotations are designed to support language-guided 3D object tracking on two mainstream LiDAR tracking benchmarks: GSOT3D and NuScenes. The dataset contains systematic natural language descriptions for tracking targets in over 1,600 scenes. Each annotation is associated with the corresponding frame, target identity, and bounding box in the original datasets. The annotations can be used to train and evaluate LiDAR-language tracking models, and to reproduce the results reported in our paper “LiDAR-Language Object Tracking via Orthogonal Slot Disentanglement.”</data>
</node>
<node id="author:haiqing ren">
  <data key="d0">Author</data>
  <data key="d1">Haiqing Ren</data>
</node>
<node id="author:hanghang chen">
