<node id="paper:W7220734184">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">"Experimental Results for Adversarially Robust Edge Intelligence Across CARLA, nuScenes, Waymo, and KITTI"</data>
  <data key="d6">"Experimental Results for Adversarially Robust Edge Intelligence Across CARLA, nuScenes, Waymo, and KITTI"</data>
  <data key="d5">2026</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.21227/4ws7-xy64</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">"This dataset contains experimental measurements developed for the evaluation of TRUST-EDGE, a defense-aware and runtime-assurance-oriented edge-intelligence framework for intelligent transportation systems. The dataset supports the quantitative assessment of machine-learning perception under benign conditions, adversarial perturbations, and edge-based defensive processing across four autonomous-driving evaluation environments: CARLA, nuScenes, the Waymo Open Dataset, and KITTI.The released Excel workbook contains both sample-level experimental observations and aggregated performance summaries. In total, the experimental data comprise 6,160 sample-level records and 28 aggregate experimental-condition records. The experiments cover clean operation and multiple adversarial conditions, includ</data>
</node>
