<node id="paper:W3037262931">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">1st Place Solution for Waymo Open Dataset Challenge -- 3D Detection and Domain Adaptation</data>
  <data key="d6">1st Place Solution for Waymo Open Dataset Challenge -- 3D Detection and Domain Adaptation</data>
  <data key="d5">2020</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2006.15505</data>
  <data key="d8">18</data>
  <data key="d9">In this technical report, we introduce our winning solution "HorizonLiDAR3D" for the 3D detection track and the domain adaptation track in Waymo Open Dataset Challenge at CVPR 2020. Many existing 3D object detectors include prior-based anchor box design to account for different scales and aspect ratios and classes of objects, which limits its capability of generalization to a different dataset or domain and requires post-processing (e.g. Non-Maximum Suppression (NMS)). We proposed a one-stage, anchor-free and NMS-free 3D point cloud object detector AFDet, using object key-points to encode the 3D attributes, and to learn an end-to-end point cloud object detection without the need of hand-engineering or learning the anchors. AFDet serves as a strong baseline in our winning solution and signi</data>
</node>
<node id="paper:W4415515001">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Investigating Fuel Consumption and Pollutants Emission of Autonomous Vehicles Using the Waymo Open Dataset</data>
  <data key="d6">Investigating Fuel Consumption and Pollutants Emission of Autonomous Vehicles Using the Waymo Open Dataset</data>
  <data key="d5">2025</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.1061/jtepbs.teeng-9066</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">Autonomous vehicles are conjectured to be environmentally friendly, but their impact on environmental sustainability is largely hypothesized or assessed via numerical simulations that do not consider driving behavior—an essential component of microscopic emission models. As such, the existing literature is devoid of any concrete evidence of autonomous vehicles’ impact on the environment using real-world data. Using the recently released Waymo open dataset, this study investigates the environmental impacts of autonomous vehicles. Specifically, microscopic fuel consumption models are employed to estimate fuel consumption and pollutant emissions (i.e., carbon dioxide, nitrogen oxide, volatile organic compounds, and particulate matter) for autonomous vehicles and compared with human-driven veh</data>
</node>
<node id="author:yasir ali">
  <data key="d0">Author</data>
  <data key="d1">Yasir Ali</data>
</node>
<node id="paper:W4406072894">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Point Transformer V3 Extreme: 1st Place Solution for 2024 Waymo Open Dataset Challenge in Semantic Segmentation</data>
  <data key="d6">Point Transformer V3 Extreme: 1st Place Solution for 2024 Waymo Open Dataset Challenge in Semantic Segmentation</data>
  <data key="d5">2024</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2407.15282</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">In this technical report, we detail our first-place solution for the 2024 Waymo Open Dataset Challenge's semantic segmentation track. We significantly enhanced the performance of Point Transformer V3 on the Waymo benchmark by implementing cutting-edge, plug-and-play training and inference technologies. Notably, our advanced version, Point Transformer V3 Extreme, leverages multi-frame training and a no-clipping-point policy, achieving substantial gains over the original PTv3 performance. Additionally, employing a straightforward model ensemble strategy further boosted our results. This approach secured us the top position on the Waymo Open Dataset semantic segmentation leaderboard, markedly outperforming other entries.</data>
</node>
