<node id="paper:W2751273146">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Generating Interpretable Images with Controllable Structure</data>
  <data key="d6">Generating Interpretable Images with Controllable Structure</data>
  <data key="d5">2017</data>
  <data key="d7"></data>
  <data key="d8">52</data>
  <data key="d9">We demonstrate improved text-to-image synthesis with controllable object locations using an extension of Pixel Convolutional Neural Networks (PixelCNN). In addition to conditioning on text, we show how the model can generate images conditioned on part keypoints and segmentation masks. The character-level text encoder and image generation network are jointly trained end-to-end via maximum likelihood. We establish quantitative baselines in terms of text and structure-conditional pixel log-likelihood for three data sets: Caltech-UCSD Birds (CUB), MPII Human Pose (MHP), and Common Objects in Context (MS-COCO).</data>
</node>
<node id="author:nal kalchbrenner">
  <data key="d0">Author</data>
  <data key="d1">Nal Kalchbrenner</data>
</node>
<node id="author:victor bapst">
  <data key="d0">Author</data>
  <data key="d1">Victor Bapst</data>
</node>
