<node id="paper:W4362706140">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Preserving Privacy in Image Database through Bit-planes Obfuscation</data>
  <data key="d6">Preserving Privacy in Image Database through Bit-planes Obfuscation</data>
  <data key="d5">2023</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.36227/techrxiv.22492714</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">We used publicly available activity recognition datasets - UCF101 and HMDB51. UCF101 - K. Soomro, A. R. Zamir, and M. Shah, “Ucf101: A dataset of 101 human actions classes from videos in the wild,” arXiv preprint arXiv:1212.0402, 2012. HMDB51 - H. Kuehne, H. Jhuang, E. Garrote, T. Poggio, and T. Serre, “Hmdb: a large video database for human motion recognition,” in Proceedings of the International Conference on Computer Vision (ICCV). IEEE, 2011, pp. 2556–2563.</data>
</node>
<node id="paper:W2580899942">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Deep Local Video Feature for Action Recognition</data>
  <data key="d6">Deep Local Video Feature for Action Recognition</data>
  <data key="d5">2017</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.1109/cvprw.2017.161</data>
  <data key="d8">118</data>
  <data key="d9">We investigate the problem of representing an entire video using CNN features for human action recognition. End-to-end learning of CNN/RNNs is currently not possible for whole videos due to GPU memory limitations and so a common practice is to use sampled frames as inputs along with the video labels as supervision. However, the global video labels might not be suitable for all of the temporally local samples as the videos often contain content besides the action of interest. We therefore propose to instead treat the deep networks trained on local inputs as local feature extractors. The local features are then aggregated to form global features which are used to assign video-level labels through a second classification stage. We investigate a number of design choices for this local feature </data>
</node>
<node id="author:zhenzhong lan">
  <data key="d0">Author</data>
  <data key="d1">Zhenzhong Lan</data>
</node>
<node id="author:yi zhu">
  <data key="d0">Author</data>
  <data key="d1">Yi Zhu</data>
</node>
