<node id="paper:W4390574409">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Channel Attention-Based Approach with Autoencoder Network for Human Action Recognition in Low-Resolution Frames</data>
  <data key="d6">Channel Attention-Based Approach with Autoencoder Network for Human Action Recognition in Low-Resolution Frames</data>
  <data key="d5">2024</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.1155/2024/1052344</data>
  <data key="d8">39</data>
  <data key="d9">Action recognition (AR) has many applications, including surveillance, health/disabilities care, man-machine interactions, video-content-based monitoring, and activity recognition. Because human action videos contain a large number of frames, implemented models must minimize computation by reducing the number, size, and resolution of frames. We propose an improved method for detecting human actions in low-size and low-resolution videos by employing convolutional neural networks (CNNs) with channel attention mechanisms (CAMs) and autoencoders (AEs). By enhancing blocks with more representative features, convolutional layers extract discriminating features from various networks. Additionally, we use random sampling of frames before main processing to improve accuracy while employing less dat</data>
</node>
<node id="author:elaheh dastbaravardeh">
  <data key="d0">Author</data>
  <data key="d1">Elaheh Dastbaravardeh</data>
</node>
