<node id="paper:W7211883695">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">"VQA-Verify"</data>
  <data key="d6">"VQA-Verify"</data>
  <data key="d5">2026</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.21227/v6jc-kx82</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">"SATORI introduces VQA-Verify, a harmonized multimodal training corpus of 12,000 samples for verifiable visual reasoning. Each instance follows a unified schema: (Image, Question, Caption, BBox, Answer), with provenance preserved from 17 source benchmarks across three task groups: Perception, Reasoning, and Multilingual. Images are paired with question-answer labels, answer-relevant bounding boxes (converted to enclosing rectangles), and captions (GPT-4o generated then manually reviewed). The dataset supports reward decomposition for RL-based multimodal training, especially caption and localization rewards in addition to format and answer correctness. VQA-Verify is designed to reduce visual grounding ambiguity in long-context multimodal reasoning and improve reproducibility through a fixed</data>
</node>
<node id="author:chu-long shen">
  <data key="d0">Author</data>
  <data key="d1">Chu-Long Shen</data>
</node>
<node id="paper:W2891021031">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Neural-Symbolic VQA: Disentangling Reasoning from Vision and Language Understanding</data>
  <data key="d6">Neural-Symbolic VQA: Disentangling Reasoning from Vision and Language Understanding</data>
  <data key="d5">2018</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.1810.02338</data>
  <data key="d8">376</data>
  <data key="d9">We marry two powerful ideas: deep representation learning for visual recognition and language understanding, and symbolic program execution for reasoning. Our neural-symbolic visual question answering (NS-VQA) system first recovers a structural scene representation from the image and a program trace from the question. It then executes the program on the scene representation to obtain an answer. Incorporating symbolic structure as prior knowledge offers three unique advantages. First, executing programs on a symbolic space is more robust to long program traces; our model can solve complex reasoning tasks better, achieving an accuracy of 99.8% on the CLEVR dataset. Second, the model is more data- and memory-efficient: it performs well after learning on a small number of training data; it can</data>
</node>
