  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">Information retrieval across different languages is an increasingly important challenge in natural language processing. Recent approaches based on multilingual pre-trained language models have achieved remarkable success, yet they often optimize for either monolingual, cross-lingual, or multilingual retrieval performance at the expense of others. This paper proposes a novel hybrid batch training strategy to simultaneously improve zero-shot retrieval performance across monolingual, cross-lingual, and multilingual settings while mitigating language bias. The approach fine-tunes multilingual lang Research goal: What is the impact of varying the proportion of monolingual, cross-lingual, and multilingual samples in hybrid batch training on inference throughput and retrieval accuracy for the Fli</data>
</node>
