  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">Since the resurgence of deep learning, vision-language models (VLMs) enhanced by large language models (LLMs) have grown exponentially in popularity. However, while LLMs can utilize extensive background knowledge and task information with in-context learning, most VLMs still struggle with understanding complex multi-modal prompts with multiple images, making VLMs less effective in downstream vision-language tasks. In this paper, we address the limitation above by 1) introducing vision-language Model with Multi-Modal In-Context Learning(MMICL), a new approach to allow the VLM to deal with multi Research goal: How does MMICL's zero-shot image-text retrieval accuracy on MSCOCO and Flickr30K compare to Flamingo, PaLI, and BLIVA when varying the number of in-context examples? Autonomous synthes</data>
