<node id="paper:W4393694388">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">ModelNet40-C</data>
  <data key="d6">ModelNet40-C</data>
  <data key="d5">2022</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.6017833</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">We create the ModelNet40-C dataset, which contains 185,100 point clouds from 40 classes, 15 corruption types, and 5 severity levels. We provide a detailed taxonomy of the constructed corruption types. ModelNet40-C is, to the best of our knowledge, the first comprehensive dataset for benchmarking corruption robustness of 3D point cloud classification. This dataset is from our arXiv paper: Benchmarking Robustness of 3D Point Cloud Recognition Against Common Corruptions.</data>
</node>
<node id="author:jiachen sun">
  <data key="d0">Author</data>
  <data key="d1">Jiachen Sun</data>
</node>
<node id="author:qingzhao zhang">
