  <data key="d6">KiDS-SQuaD</data>
  <data key="d5">2019</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.1051/0004-6361/201936006</data>
  <data key="d8">45</data>
  <data key="d9">Context.The KiDS Strongly lensed QUAsar Detection project (KiDS-SQuaD) is aimed at finding as many previously undiscovered gravitational lensed quasars as possible in the Kilo Degree Survey. This is the second paper of this series where we present a new, automatic object-classification method based on the machine learning technique. Aims.The main goal of this paper is to build a catalogue of bright extragalactic objects (galaxies and quasars) from the KiDS Data Release 4, with minimum stellar contamination and preserving the completeness as much as possible. We show here that this catalogue represents the perfect starting point to search for reliable gravitationally lensed quasar candidates. Methods.After testing some of the most used machine learning algorithms, decision-tree-based classi</data>
