<node id="paper:W2109275023">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Immunolocalization ofLeishmania (Viannia) braziliensismembrane antigens recognized by mAbs SST-2, SST-3, and SST-4</data>
  <data key="d6">Immunolocalization ofLeishmania (Viannia) braziliensismembrane antigens recognized by mAbs SST-2, SST-3, and SST-4</data>
  <data key="d5">2003</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.1017/s0031182003003986</data>
  <data key="d8">5</data>
  <data key="d9">The immunolocalization of Leishmania (Viannia) braziliensis stage-specific antigens recognized by mAbs was analysed by transmission electron microscopy. The antigen recognized by mAb SST-2 was present at the surface of promastigotes, including the flagellum and flagellar pocket. The reactivity of SST-2 with isolates of different serodemes showed a pronounced microheterogeneity in terms of the number of reactive bands within the low molecular weight range from 24 to 33 kDa. The 180 kDa glycoprotein recognized by mAb SST-3 was present only in the flagellar membrane. SST-3 also recognized multiple discrete bands from 160 to 200 kDa, as observed in several serodemes. In contrast, mAb SST-4, which recognizes a 98 kDa antigen, showed weak labelling on the promastigote surface by transmission ele</data>
</node>
