<node id="paper:W7163657725">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Sentiment Analysis on IMDB Reviews: A Comparative Study of Bag-of-Words, Deep Learning, and Transformer Models</data>
  <data key="d6">Sentiment Analysis on IMDB Reviews: A Comparative Study of Bag-of-Words, Deep Learning, and Transformer Models</data>
  <data key="d5">2026</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.1109/aide69088.2026.11544304</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">Sentiment Analysis (SA) on film reviews can provide filmmakers, distributors, and content providers with information about how audiences perceive or feel about a movie before its release. The growing prevalence of web-based critiques necessitates sentiment classification to better understand audience perceptions of films immediately after reviews are written or published. This research offers a detailed comparison of multiple machine learning (ML), deep learning (DL), and transformer-based approaches. These techniques are applied to sentiment classification using the IMDB film review dataset. The study utilizes Bag-of-Words, TF-IDF, and GloVe embeddings. It also examines transformer architectures such as BART and Longformer. The findings indicate that transformer-based approaches achieve s</data>
</node>
