<node id="paper:W2279409141">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Effective 20 Newsgroups Dataset Cleaning</data>
  <data key="d6">Effective 20 Newsgroups Dataset Cleaning</data>
  <data key="d5">2015</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.1109/wi-iat.2015.90</data>
  <data key="d8">38</data>
  <data key="d9">The rapid increase in the number of text documents available on the Internet has created pressure to use effective cleaning techniques. Cleaning techniques are needed for converting these documents to structured documents. Text cleaning techniques are one of the key mechanisms in typical text mining application frameworks. In this paper, we explore the role of text cleaning in the 20 newsgroups dataset, and report on experimental results.</data>
</node>
