<node id="paper:W4252110927">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Proceedings of the seventh conference on Natural language learning at HLT-NAACL 2003 -</data>
  <data key="d6">Proceedings of the seventh conference on Natural language learning at HLT-NAACL 2003 -</data>
  <data key="d5">2003</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.3115/1119176</data>
  <data key="d8">123</data>
  <data key="d9">This volume contains the papers accepted for presentation at the 2003 conference on Computational Natural Language Learning (CoNLL-2003), a SIGNLL meeting held in Edmonton, Canada, May 31 and June 1 in conjunction with the HLT-NAACL Conference.</data>
</node>
<node id="paper:W2949990951">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">A New Concept of Deep Reinforcement Learning based Augmented General Sequence Tagging System</data>
  <data key="d6">A New Concept of Deep Reinforcement Learning based Augmented General Sequence Tagging System</data>
  <data key="d5">2018</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.1812.10234</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
  <data key="d9">In this paper, a new deep reinforcement learning based augmented general sequence tagging system is proposed. The new system contains two parts: a deep neural network (DNN) based sequence tagging model and a deep reinforcement learning (DRL) based augmented tagger. The augmented tagger helps improve system performance by modeling the data with minority tags. The new system is evaluated on SLU and NLU sequence tagging tasks using ATIS and CoNLL-2003 benchmark datasets, to demonstrate the new system's outstanding performance on general tagging tasks. Evaluated by F1 scores, it shows that the new system outperforms the current state-of-the-art model on ATIS dataset by 1.9% and that on CoNLL-2003 dataset by 1.4%.</data>
</node>
<node id="author:abhishek patel">
  <data key="d0">Author</data>
  <data key="d1">Abhishek Patel</data>
</node>
<node id="author:hongxia jin">
