<node id="paper:W7124940462">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">PampaR: Cerebral Language Model with Territorial Architecture</data>
  <data key="d6">PampaR: Cerebral Language Model with Territorial Architecture</data>
  <data key="d5">2026</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.18315642</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">PampaR is a brain-inspired language model that achieves perplexity ~45 with only 14M parameters on WikiText-103. It uses a novel territorial architecture with 4 specialized territories (Expressive, Contextual, Formal, Structural) coordinated by a central Thalamus using hybrid routing: 70% explicit rules (LLAVES) + 30% learned attention. Trained entirely on consumer hardware (GTX 1650 4GB VRAM).</data>
</node>
<node id="author:lucas ricardo mella chillemi">
