<node id="paper:W7203473722">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">What Survives the Controls? Derived data, pre-registrations, and findings ledger</data>
  <data key="d6">What Survives the Controls? Derived data, pre-registrations, and findings ledger</data>
  <data key="d5">2026</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.21929972</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">Derived data supporting a pre-registered audit of internal-state and sampling-based hallucination detection. Contains 41 derived result tables (CSV) from which every number, table and figure in the accompanying article is computed; the three pre-registrations as registered, stating hypotheses and decision criteria before the corresponding runs; and the complete findings ledger, including superseded, post-hoc and void entries with what killed them. Measurements cover three small decoder-only instruction-tuned language models (Gemma-2-2B, Llama-3.2-3B, Qwen2.5-7B) on CNN/DailyMail, XSum, and the XSum-Hallucination annotations, seeded throughout. The analysis code is released separately at https://github.com/mudasirmohd/geosumm-battery, from which all published tables and figures regenerate f</data>
</node>
