</node>
<node id="paper:W2119760551">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">CUNI in WMT14: Chimera Still Awaits Bellerophon</data>
  <data key="d6">CUNI in WMT14: Chimera Still Awaits Bellerophon</data>
  <data key="d5">2014</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.3115/v1/w14-3322</data>
  <data key="d8">7</data>
  <data key="d9">We present our English→Czech and\nEnglish→Hindi submissions for this\nyear’s WMT translation task. For\nEnglish→Czech, we build upon last year’s\nCHIMERA and evaluate several setups.\nEnglish→Hindi is a new language pair for\nthis year. We experimented with reverse\nself-training to acquire more (synthetic)\nparallel data and with modeling target-side\nmorphology.</data>
</node>
<node id="author:aleš tamchyna">
  <data key="d0">Author</data>
  <data key="d1">Aleš Tamchyna</data>
</node>
<node id="author:martin popel">
  <data key="d0">Author</data>
  <data key="d1">Martin Popel</data>
</node>
<node id="author:rudolf rosa">
  <data key="d0">Author</data>
  <data key="d1">Rudolf Rosa</data>
</node>
<node id="paper:W2336605602">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Russian-English Machine Translation System for WMT14</data>
  <data key="d6">Russian-English Machine Translation System for WMT14</data>
  <data key="d5">2014</data>
  <data key="d7"></data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">This paper describes the Yandex School of Data Analysis Russian-English system submitted to the ACL 2014 Ninth Workshop on Statistical Machine Translation shared translation task. We start with the system that we developed last year and investigate a few methods that were successful at the previous translation task including unpruned language model, operation sequence model and the new reparameterization of IBM Model 2. Next we propose a {simple yet practical} algorithm to transform Russian sentence into a more easily translatable form before decoding. The algorithm is based on the linguistic intuition of native Russian speakers, also fluent in English.</data>
</node>
