<node id="paper:W3198002980">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Finetuned Language Models Are Zero-Shot Learners</data>
  <data key="d6">Finetuned Language Models Are Zero-Shot Learners</data>
  <data key="d5">2021</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2109.01652</data>
  <data key="d8">1098</data>
  <data key="d9">This paper explores a simple method for improving the zero-shot learning abilities of language models. We show that instruction tuning -- finetuning language models on a collection of tasks described via instructions -- substantially improves zero-shot performance on unseen tasks. We take a 137B parameter pretrained language model and instruction-tune it on over 60 NLP tasks verbalized via natural language instruction templates. We evaluate this instruction-tuned model, which we call FLAN, on unseen task types. FLAN substantially improves the performance of its unmodified counterpart and surpasses zero-shot 175B GPT-3 on 20 of 25 tasks that we evaluate. FLAN even outperforms few-shot GPT-3 by a large margin on ANLI, RTE, BoolQ, AI2-ARC, OpenbookQA, and StoryCloze. Ablation studies reveal t</data>
</node>
