  <data key="d5">2023</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.7765139</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">Introduction Librispeech Slakh Unmix (LSX) is a proof of concept source separation dataset for training and testing algorithms that separate a monaural audio signal using hyperbolic embeddings for hierarchical separation. The dataset is composed of artificial mixtures using audio from the librispeech (clean subset) and Slakh2100 datasets. The dataset was introduced in our paper Hyperbolic Audio Source Separation. At a Glance The size of the unzipped dataset is ~28GB Each mixture is 60-s in length and denotes the first 60 s of the bass, drums, and guitar stems of the associated Slakh2100 track. Audio is encoded as 16 bit wav files at a sampling rate of 16 kHz The data is split into training tr (1390 mixtues), validation cv (348 mixtures) and testing tt (209 mixtures) subsets The directory f</data>
</node>
