<node id="paper:W4294437546">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Identifying Films with Noir Characteristics Using Audience's Tags on MovieLens</data>
  <data key="d6">Identifying Films with Noir Characteristics Using Audience's Tags on MovieLens</data>
  <data key="d5">2022</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2209.00447</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">We consider the noir classification problem by exploring noir attributes and what films are likely to be regarded as noirish from the perspective of a wide Internet audience. We use a dataset consisting of more than 30,000 films with relevant tags added by users of MovieLens, a web-based recommendation system. Based on this data, we develop a statistical model to identify films with noir characteristics using these free-form tags. After retrieving information for describing films from tags, we implement a one-class nearest neighbors algorithm to recognize noirish films by learning from IMDb-labeled noirs. Our analysis evidences film noirs' close relationship with German Expressionism, French Poetic Realism, British thrillers, and American pre-code crime pictures, revealing the similarities</data>
</node>
