<node id="paper:W7143382971">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">MovieLens 32M for Property Graph Benchmark</data>
  <data key="d6">MovieLens 32M for Property Graph Benchmark</data>
  <data key="d5">2026</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.7910/dvn/4en5js</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">This dataset is adpated from MovieLens 32M dataset: https://grouplens.org/datasets/movielens/32m/. We added some files for faster data import into graph database systems. However, some of the original files were also used for data import so we kept them in this repository as well. Here are the descriptions of the added files: 1. genre_vertices.csv (Genre vertices) o Extracted unique genre names from the pipe-delimited genres column in movies.csv o Split multi-genre entries (e.g., "Comedy|Romance") into individual genre vertices o Filtered out null and empty genre values 2. has_genre.csv (HAS_GENRE edges) o Created edges linking each movie to its associated genres o Structure: src (movieId) → dst (genre name) o Derived from the same genre extraction process 3. clean_ratings_df.csv (User ver</data>
</node>
