  <data key="d1">Enhancing Sentiment Insights from Amazon Reviews</data>
  <data key="d6">Enhancing Sentiment Insights from Amazon Reviews</data>
  <data key="d5">2025</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.1109/icssas66150.2025.11080845</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">In recent times, the drastic growth of the e-commerce scenario has brought up tremendous volumes of product reviews; most especially for Amazon. While knowing what their customers feel could be important enough for a customer, it is for any business. The study in this paper involves machine and deep learning methods, for performing the task of the sentiment analysis over Amazon review products. We implemented different algorithms, including SVM and Naive Bayes to LSTM networks and Convolutional Neural Networks. It contains a dataset of reviews of various products that are pre-processed for tasks like noise removal and removing irrelevant information. Sentiment labels are assigned based on the review ratings, allowing us to train our models effectively. The evaluation of each model is done </data>
</node>
