  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">This is an adapted version of the Yelp Open Dataset. Here is the original publishing site: https://business.yelp.com/data/resources/open-dataset/. We modified the json file structures so that it can be easily read and uploaded to graph database systems, such as Neo4j and TigerGraph. All the files with names like "yelp_academic_dataset_xxx.json” can be downloaded directly from yelp’s website. We also added here because for our benchmark project these files are still needed for uploading to some specific database systems. Here are some detailed processing steps we took to transform the original dataset: category_vertices.json (Category vertices) 1. Extracted unique business categories from the categories field in yelp_academic_dataset_business.json 2. Removed duplicate category entries (the </data>
