<node id="paper:W7111910311">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Predicting Customer Sentiment and Purchase Intent with Neural Networks : Experiments using Yelp</data>
  <data key="d6">Predicting Customer Sentiment and Purchase Intent with Neural Networks : Experiments using Yelp</data>
  <data key="d5">2025</data>
  <data key="d7"></data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">This thesis investigates whether neural networks can classify sentiment in customer reviews and predict purchase intent from review text using the Yelp Open Dataset. The study compares three models: a TF-IDF plus linear baseline, a long short-term memory (LSTM) network with Global Vectors for Word Representation (GloVe) embeddings, and a fine-tuned DistilBERT transformer. Preprocessing includes text normalization through lower casing, emoji and URL removal, lemmatization, and contraction handling, as well as stratified train, validation, and test splits. Since the Yelp dataset does not provide intent labels, intent is constructed using a weak to-gold labeling strategy. Heuristic cue phrases generate weak labels at scale, and a subset is manually annotated using a Jupyter interface. Final l</data>
</node>
<node id="author:adeyemo, adewale">
  <data key="d0">Author</data>
  <data key="d1">Adeyemo, Adewale</data>
</node>
<node id="paper:W3097446167">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">"You eat with your eyes first": Optimizing Yelp Image Advertising</data>
  <data key="d6">"You eat with your eyes first": Optimizing Yelp Image Advertising</data>
  <data key="d5">2020</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2011.01434</data>
  <data key="d8">1</data>
  <data key="d9">A business's online, photographic representation can play a crucial role in its success or failure. We use Yelp's image dataset and star-based review system as a measurement of an image's effectiveness in promoting a business. After preprocessing the Yelp dataset, we use transfer learning to train a classifier which accepts Yelp images and predicts star-ratings. Additionally, we then train a GAN to qualitatively investigate the common properties of highly effective images. We achieve 90-98% accuracy in classifying simplified star ratings for various image categories and observe that images containing blue skies, open surroundings, and many windows are correlated with higher Yelp reviews.</data>
</node>
