  <data key="d8">2</data>
  <data key="d9">The use of a health big data via Medical Information Mart for Intensive Care (MIMIC) data sets has significant advancements in health informatics and clinical research of electronic health records (EHRs) in hospital systems. MIMIC-III and MIMIC-IV data sets are the two latest publicly available iterations of data from electronic records that possess distinct features, variables, and structures in two separate large relational databases. This study aimed to provide big data analytics comparisons of MIMIC-III and MIMIC-IV for experiential learning of health informatics from EHRs.Both data sets were quantitatively and qualitatively evaluated based on dataset properties (data, list of tables, timeline, patient encounters, software, system), data mining and visual categories (i.e., data size, d</data>
