<node id="paper:W3188252230">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">RadGraph: Extracting Clinical Entities and Relations from Radiology Reports</data>
  <data key="d6">RadGraph: Extracting Clinical Entities and Relations from Radiology Reports</data>
  <data key="d5">2021</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.48550/arxiv.2106.14463</data>
  <data key="d8">90</data>
  <data key="d9">Extracting structured clinical information from free-text radiology reports can enable the use of radiology report information for a variety of critical healthcare applications. In our work, we present RadGraph, a dataset of entities and relations in full-text chest X-ray radiology reports based on a novel information extraction schema we designed to structure radiology reports. We release a development dataset, which contains board-certified radiologist annotations for 500 radiology reports from the MIMIC-CXR dataset (14,579 entities and 10,889 relations), and a test dataset, which contains two independent sets of board-certified radiologist annotations for 100 radiology reports split equally across the MIMIC-CXR and CheXpert datasets. Using these datasets, we train and test a deep learni</data>
</node>
