<node id="paper:W7139912954">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Transfer Learning with ResNet-50 for Multi-Label Chest X-Ray Classification on the NIH ChestX-Ray14 Dataset</data>
  <data key="d6">Transfer Learning with ResNet-50 for Multi-Label Chest X-Ray Classification on the NIH ChestX-Ray14 Dataset</data>
  <data key="d5">2025</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.1109/acoit66109.2025.11437206</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">Early and correct diagnosis of several lung diseases based on chest X-rays is crucial to the proper management of patients. The current methods are more likely to miss comorbidities, are linked to unbalanced data problems, and cannot be understood clinically. This paper introduces a transfer learning system on ResNet-50 to classify multiple labels with the NIH ChestX-ray14 dataset. It is proposed to use preprocessing, data augmentation, and residual block feature extraction followed by thresholded multi-label prediction to achieve good results. The experimentally obtained results are more accurate (94.6%), recollective (91.1%), F1-score (0.917) and AUC (0.97), whereas Inference times are less; this attributes to its efficiency and suitability. The framework is a feasible and scalable appro</data>
</node>
