<node id="paper:W7213654179">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Curated Patient-Wise Pneumothorax versus No Finding Cohort with Visible-Device Annotations Derived from NIH ChestX-ray14</data>
  <data key="d6">Curated Patient-Wise Pneumothorax versus No Finding Cohort with Visible-Device Annotations Derived from NIH ChestX-ray14</data>
  <data key="d5">2026</data>
  <data key="d7">https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22839697</data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">This research-data and reproducibility package contains the derived cohort manifest, fixed patient-wise split, visible-device annotations, annotation quality-control provenance, locked prediction exports, and statistical analysis artifacts used in a study of visible medical devices as potential confounders in deep-learning pneumothorax classification. The curated cohort contains 4,388 radiographs from 3,128 patients (2,194 Pneumothorax and 2,194 No Finding). Train, validation, and frozen-test partitions have zero patient overlap. Original NIH ChestX-ray14 radiographs are not redistributed; users must obtain the source images from the official NIH distribution and reconstruct the cohort using the released image identifiers.</data>
</node>
