<node id="paper:arxiv:2506.18535v1">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">When Fine-Tuning Fails: Lessons from MS MARCO Passage Ranking</data>
  <data key="d6">When Fine-Tuning Fails: Lessons from MS MARCO Passage Ranking</data>
  <data key="d5">2025</data>
  <data key="d7"></data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">This paper investigates the counterintuitive phenomenon where fine-tuning pre-trained transformer models degrades performance on the MS MARCO passage ranking task. Through comprehensive experiments involving five model variants-including full parameter fine-tuning and parameter efficient LoRA adaptations-we demonstrate that all fine-tuning approaches underperform the base sentence-transformers/all- MiniLM-L6-v2 model (MRR@10: 0.3026). Our analysis reveals that fine-tuning disrupts the optimal embedding space structure learned during the base model's extensive pre-training on 1 billion sentence pairs, including 9.1 million MS MARCO samples. UMAP visualizations show progressive embedding space flattening, while training dynamics analysis and computational efficiency metrics further support o</data>
</node>
<node id="author:manu pande">
  <data key="d0">Author</data>
  <data key="d1">Manu Pande</data>
</node>
<node id="author:shahil kumar">
  <data key="d0">Author</data>
  <data key="d1">Shahil Kumar</data>
</node>
<node id="author:anay yatin damle">
  <data key="d0">Author</data>
  <data key="d1">Anay Yatin Damle</data>
</node>
<node id="paper:arxiv:2009.09392v1">
  <data key="d0">Paper</data>
  <data key="d1">Longformer for MS MARCO Document Re-ranking Task</data>
  <data key="d6">Longformer for MS MARCO Document Re-ranking Task</data>
  <data key="d5">2020</data>
  <data key="d7"></data>
  <data key="d8">0</data>
  <data key="d9">Two step document ranking, where the initial retrieval is done by a classical information retrieval method, followed by neural re-ranking model, is the new standard. The best performance is achieved by using transformer-based models as re-rankers, e.g., BERT. We employ Longformer, a BERT-like model for long documents, on the MS MARCO document re-ranking task. The complete code used for training the model can be found on: https://github.com/isekulic/longformer-marco</data>
</node>
<node id="author:ivan sekulić">
  <data key="d0">Author</data>
  <data key="d1">Ivan Sekulić</data>
</node>
<node id="author:amir soleimani">
  <data key="d0">Author</data>
  <data key="d1">Amir Soleimani</data>
</node>
